      "start_seconds": 1.23,
      "end_seconds": 6.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "I mean, um, hello, doctor. I think it's my turn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.23,
      "end_seconds": 13.42,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "You're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.52,
      "end_seconds": 24.19,
      "duration_seconds": 8.67,
      "text": "Uh, mainly some bleeding. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.15,
      "end_seconds": 29.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "When was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.81,
      "end_seconds": 34.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "For about a week, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.05,
      "end_seconds": 38.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Have you been feeling sick in the mornings?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.68,
      "end_seconds": 60.8,
      "duration_seconds": 16.12,
      "text": "Yes, since Monday. Sorry, what was I saying, and there's cramping in my lower tummy as well, three days now. With cramping in my lower tummy, only rest, and it's not much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.76,
      "end_seconds": 63.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "I'll do your observations first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.45,
      "end_seconds": 76.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.3,
      "end_seconds": 94.96,
      "duration_seconds": 8.66,
      "text": "Okay: heart rate 77, SpO2 98 percent on room air. And temperature is 36.6 degrees, BP is 119 over 68."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.08,
      "end_seconds": 97.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.38,
      "end_seconds": 102.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Don't worry, we'll discuss it in a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.77,
      "end_seconds": 123.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Did you get fainting or severe one-sided pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.7,
      "end_seconds": 126.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "No, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.77,
      "end_seconds": 130.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Did you notice any passing tissue?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.18,
      "end_seconds": 135.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "No. No passing tissue."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.82,
      "end_seconds": 140.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Any muscle or joint problems besides this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.93,
      "end_seconds": 142.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.8,
      "end_seconds": 149.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Anything on the skin I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.37,
      "end_seconds": 152.36,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "Skin's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.79,
      "end_seconds": 156.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Does your family have any medical conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.03,
      "end_seconds": 160.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "My grandfather had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.74,
      "end_seconds": 165.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.0,
      "end_seconds": 170.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Naproxen, 250 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.18,
      "end_seconds": 174.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.24,
      "end_seconds": 182.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "I've never had an allergy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.86,
      "end_seconds": 203.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.28,
      "end_seconds": 222.05,
      "duration_seconds": 13.77,
      "text": "Hmm, yes, arthritis in my knees. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.7,
      "end_seconds": 232.77,
      "duration_seconds": 9.07,
      "text": "Okay, I can see arthritis in your knees in your file as well. Have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.49,
      "end_seconds": 238.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Just part of my thyroid removed, years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.14,
      "end_seconds": 258.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.56,
      "end_seconds": 267.99,
      "duration_seconds": 8.43,
      "text": "I swim twice a week. I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day. My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.63,
      "end_seconds": 287.73,
      "duration_seconds": 18.1,
      "text": "Let me tell you where I've got to. It points towards bleeding in early pregnancy that needs a scan. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. I can't rule out a threatened miscarriage yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 289.49,
      "end_seconds": 292.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Let me think, is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.33,
      "end_seconds": 325.25,
      "duration_seconds": 30.92,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's bleeding in early pregnancy that needs a scan, and we'll know more once the a pregnancy hormone level is back. A pregnancy hormone level is what I'd like next, for bleeding in early pregnancy. Use pads rather than tampons and avoid intercourse until the scan. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.08,
      "end_seconds": 328.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}